  "coverage_limit": "granit_parser::Parser::new_from_str event stream on local UTF-8 text with exactly one document required; the harness assembles the typed tree from the events, copies the anchored node for each Alias event, skips Comment/Anchor metadata events, and types plain scalars with the YAML 1.2 core-schema patterns (null, bool, int, float, otherwise str) as the C and C++ YAML harnesses do; quoted and block scalars are str. granit-parser is a fork of saphyr-parser (yaml-rust lineage). Mapping keys must be untagged scalars. The schema-neutral controls do not test tags, merge keys, multi-document streams or YAML 1.1-only scalars.",
  "afl_monomorphization_shim": "src/events (parsarium_yaml_granit_parser_events) only instantiates granit_parser::Parser<StrInput>; Rust compiles generic code into the instantiating crate, so without the shim the parser's scanner and parser were compiled into the uninstrumented harness crate. The shim is instrumented with the parser crates; the harness's tree builder and scalar typing stay uninstrumented."
